      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "From two heads to one: Electoral and governance consequences of political recentralization",
      "title_cn": "从两个头到一个头：政治再集权的选举与治理后果",
      "authors": [
        "Olivier Marie",
        "Thomas Post",
        "Zihan Ye",
        "Xiaopeng Zou"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "The consequences of retracting democratic rights in authoritarian regimes remain understudied. In 2018, China’s Communist Party implemented the ‘one-head’ policy, replacing dual village governance with a single leader. Using nationally representative survey data and exploiting the exogeneity of village election cycles as an instrument, we analyze short-term effects on voting behavior and political perceptions. Villages adopting the one-head system experienced a sizable decline in election turnout. At the same time, villagers reported lower perceived corruption and greater confidence in local governance. In addition, we find supporting evidence based on changes in objective economic indicators. These results suggest that recentralization reduced electoral participation but did not erode, and may have improved, (perceived) governance quality in the short run.",
      "abstract_cn": "关于威权政体收回民主权利的后果，研究仍然不足。在2018年，中国共产党实施了“一肩挑”政策，以单一领导人取代双元村庄治理。我们使用全国代表性调查数据，并利用村庄选举周期的外生性作为工具变量，分析其对投票行为和政治认知的短期影响。采用一肩挑制度的村庄选举投票率出现了大幅下降。与此同时，村民报告的感知腐败程度更低，对地方治理的信心更高。此外，我们还基于客观经济指标的变化发现了支持性证据。这些结果表明，再集权降低了选举参与，但并未削弱，且可能在短期内改善了（感知的）治理质量。",
